request: Make the output easier to read.

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" is subjective and can't be tested as written. Any change to the rendered text will probably break existing format tests, which I'd have to approve, so I need to know which specific changes are wanted before I break current behaviour.)
governor asks: What would make the todo list output easier to read for you? Please pick any of these, or describe your own:
1. Status markers: show done and open items with clear checkboxes, e.g. "[x]" and "[ ]".
2. Aligned columns: pad IDs and titles so they line up, e.g. "  3. [ ] Buy milk        (due 2024-05-01)".
3. Due dates: show them in a consistent spot with a label like "due: 2024-05-01", and leave them out when there's no date.
4. Empty list: show a friendly message such as "No todos." instead of blank output.
5. Grouping or summary: list open items before done ones, and/or add a footer like "2 open, 1 done".
6. Colour: use terminal colours, e.g. dim the done items and turn overdue dates red.
Also, should this apply only to `list`, or to the confirmation text after `add`/`complete` as well? If you can, paste an example of the exact output you'd like.

